<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Stock overview</title><style>body{font:13px system-ui,sans-serif;color:#111;margin:24px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:8px;border:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left;overflow-wrap:anywhere}thead{display:table-header-group}tr{break-inside:avoid}h1{font-size:22px}@page{size:A4 landscape;margin:12mm}@media print{button{display:none}}</style><body><button onclick="window.print()">Print / Save as PDF</button><h1>{{ $business->name }} — Stock overview</h1><p>{{ now()->format('Y-m-d H:i') }} · {{ $business->currency }}</p><p>Quantity stock uses current catalogue cost estimates. Serialized stock uses recorded device costs. These figures are not an accounting inventory valuation.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Location</th><th>Product / variant / SKU</th><th>Quantity</th><th>Retail value</th>@if($costs)<th>Cost estimate</th>@endif</tr></thead><tbody>@foreach($rows as $row)<tr><td>{{ $row->location }}</td><td>{{ $row->product }} · {{ $row->variant }}<br>{{ $row->sku }}</td><td>{{ $row->quantity }}</td><td>{{ number_format($row->retail_value,2) }}</td>@if($costs)<td>{{ number_format($row->cost_value,2) }}</td>@endif</tr>@endforeach</tbody></table></body></html>